WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.785
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit
2: Celebrations and Festivals.

2
00:00:04.865 --> 00:00:10.886
In this unit you will explore celebrations
and festivals from around the world,

3
00:00:10.966 --> 00:00:17.990
with a special focus on traditions that matter
to communities across East Africa and beyond.

4
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.461
Festivals bring people together.

5
00:00:20.541 --> 00:00:27.257
They remind us of our history, our values,
and the things that make each culture unique.

6
00:00:27.337 --> 00:00:35.134
Whether it is the joy of a national independence
day, the colourful lanterns of a harvest celebration,

7
00:00:35.214 --> 00:00:41.002
or the excitement of a local sports
day, every festival has a story to tell.

8
00:00:41.082 --> 00:00:47.489
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:47.569 --> 00:00:56.316
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand texts about different festivals and celebrations.

10
00:00:56.396 --> 00:01:02.820
You will also use prepositions of time (in,
on, at) correctly in speech and writing.

11
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:09.324
You will also recognise and form compound
adjectives (hand-made, brightly coloured).

12
00:01:09.404 --> 00:01:12.189
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:12.269 --> 00:01:19.846
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: benevolent,
charismatic, determined, diligent, enthusiastic, industrious.

14
00:01:19.926 --> 00:01:25.058
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:25.138 --> 00:01:29.112
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:29.192 --> 00:01:37.151
The reading sequence includes Festivals That Bring Us
Together, part 1 and Festivals That Bring Us Together, part 2.

17
00:01:37.231 --> 00:01:38.122
Read actively.

18
00:01:38.202 --> 00:01:42.903
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:47.408
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:47.488 --> 00:01:52.217
The first language focus is
Prepositions of Time: In, On and At.

21
00:01:52.297 --> 00:01:59.880
Prepositions of time tell your reader exactly when
something happens: in holds long stretches of time,

22
00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:05.290
on lands on particular days and dates,
and at points to precise moments.

23
00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:13.480
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.141
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Compare Two Festivals.

25
00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:22.945
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:23.025 --> 00:02:26.603
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:26.683 --> 00:02:30.403
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.225
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:32.305 --> 00:02:40.065
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:40.145 --> 00:02:43.867
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:43.947 --> 00:02:52.816
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
